 "questions": [
  {
   "id": 545750,
   "is_answer_order_important": false,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "Using the data in Example 13.5, how much water would be saved in a year if one-sixth of the population of the state of Florida, which is approximately 21.6 million people, turned the faucet off when brushing their teeth except when rinsing for a year (52 weeks)?",
   "answers": [],
   "hints": [],
   "formats": [
    "free-response"
   ],
   "combo_choices": [],
   "collaborator_solutions": [
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "summary",
     "content_html": "<p>Find one-sixth of the population of Florida (21.6 million people).</p>\n<p><span data-math=\"\\frac{1}{6}\\left( {21,600,000} \\right) = 3,600,000{\\rm{\\ people}}\"></span></p>\n<p>Find the savings for one person in a year.</p>\n<p>Gallons used if leave water on:</p>\n<p><span data-math=\"\\frac{{{\\rm{4\\ gallons}}}}{{\\cancel{{{\\rm{brushing}}}}}}\\left( {\\frac{{2\\cancel{{{\\rm{brushings}}}}}}{{{\\rm{day}}}}} \\right)\\left( {\\frac{{7\\cancel{{{\\rm{days}}}}}}{{\\cancel{{{\\rm{week}}}}}}} \\right)\\left( {\\frac{{52\\cancel{{{\\rm{weeks}}}}}}{{{\\rm{year}}}}} \\right) = 2,912\\frac{{{\\rm{gallons}}}}{{{\\rm{year}}}}\"></span></p>\n<p>Gallons used if turn water off:</p>\n<p><span data-math=\"\\frac{{{\\rm{0}}{\\rm{.25\\ gallons}}}}{{\\cancel{{{\\rm{brushing}}}}}}\\left( {\\frac{{2\\cancel{{{\\rm{brushings}}}}}}{{{\\rm{day}}}}} \\right)\\left( {\\frac{{7\\cancel{{{\\rm{days}}}}}}{{\\cancel{{{\\rm{week}}}}}}} \\right)\\left( {52\\frac{{\\cancel{{{\\rm{weeks}}}}}}{{{\\rm{year}}}}} \\right) = 364\\frac{{{\\rm{gallons}}}}{{{\\rm{year}}}}\"></span></p>\n<p>Find the difference: 2,912 – 364 = 2,548 gallons saved per year per person.</p>\n<p><span data-math=\"3,600,000\\cancel{{{\\rm{people}}}}\\left( {\\frac{{2,548{\\rm{\\ gallons}}}}{{1{\\rm{ }}\\cancel{{{\\rm{person}}}}}}} \\right) = 9,172,800,000{\\rm{\\ people}}\"></span></p>\n<p>The town would save around 9.828 million gallons per year.</p>"
    },
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "detailed",
     "content_html": "9,828 million gal of water"
    }
   ],
